context:
Quest Banket.qmm: locations.43.texts.0.text. Preserve every <tag> exactly. English reference: - Excellent! Here you go. The recipe couldn't be simpler - take some <clr>white shabby-lee whine<clrEnd> and add the same amount of other components so that the relative composition of the main properties was optimised. Oh yes, I forgot to say that for Maloq moonshiners the quality of alcohol drinks is determined by the relative composition of <clr>three<clrEnd> main properties - <clr>strength<clrEnd>, or alcohol containing, level of <clr>transparency<clrEnd> and specific <clr>carbonation<clrEnd>. 

For instance a quality Chins is supposed to be <clr>55 percent<clrEnd> plus strong, have a TRANSPARENCY of <clr>80%<clrEnd> and its CARBONATION is not to exceed <clr>10 units<clrEnd>.

The used components are:

 - diethylmethylchlorane repusator, or simply <clr>repusator<clrEnd>, which I used to dissolve bubbles of air;
- pasteurised hydrogen oxide, the so-called <clr>boiled water<clrEnd> - used to dilute strong and dark drinks;
- hiphops root tincture, also known as <clr>hiphops<clrEnd> - the alcohol-containing juice of this plant is dark in colour;
